    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35-a2">

                <pb facs="0081" n="815" xml:id="pg815"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 149.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Smythe to Mr. Faine.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-22"><hi rendition="#italic">May 22,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your verbal communication at our last
                    interview to the effect that your office sustained the seizure of an installment
                    of Mr. Allen’s indemnity money while in transit to this legation has been the
                    subject of thought and investigation, and I am convinced that it would be in
                    derogation to the dignity of my Government and of yours to permit any
                    interference with the terms of the agreement entered into between your office
                    and this legation. If that is still your opinion, be kind enough to put it in
                    writing, so that I can transmit it to my Government for instruction.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry M. Smythe.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
